summary:
  A wall clock that lands before the alarm's fire leaves the alarm ringing.

history:
  The half hour is counted on the wall clock, which a time sync or a
  changed zone can move. Set back behind the fire, the difference is
  negative and passes any upper bound: the alarm would ring for as long as
  the clock took to catch up, hours for a zone change.

target:
  package/contents/ui/AlarmLogic.js

find:
      if (nowMs < firedAtMs) return false;

replace:
      if (nowMs < 0) return false;

expect:
  Killed by tst_alarmlogic::test_a_clock_that_jumped_ends_the_ringing_and_cannot_lengthen_it.
  Line-neutral.
